questions.question:
Let z be a complex number with non-zero imaginary part. If
\frac{2+3z+4z^2}{2-3z+4z^2}
is a real number, then the value of \(|z|^2\) is ________.

questions.explanation:
Given that
z \neq \bar{z}
Let \(\alpha = \frac{2+3z+4z^2}{2-3z+4z^2} = \frac{(2-3z+4z^2)+6z}{2-3z+4z^2}\)
\therefore \alpha = 1 + \frac{6z}{2-3z+4z^2}
If \(\alpha\) is a real number, then
\alpha = \bar{\alpha}
\implies 1 + \frac{6z}{2-3z+4z^2} = 1 + \frac{6\bar{z}}{2-3\bar{z}+4\bar{z}^2}
\implies \frac{z}{2-3z+4z^2} = \frac{\bar{z}}{2-3\bar{z}+4\bar{z}^2}
\implies z(2-3\bar{z}+4\bar{z}^2) = \bar{z}(2-3z+4z^2)
\implies 2z - 3z\bar{z} + 4z\bar{z}^2 = 2\bar{z} - 3z\bar{z} + 4\bar{z}z^2
\implies 2z + 4z\bar{z}^2 = 2\bar{z} + 4\bar{z}z^2
\implies 2(z-\bar{z}) = 4z\bar{z}(z-\bar{z})
\implies (z-\bar{z})(2-4z\bar{z}) = 0
As \(z \neq \bar{z}\) (Given)
\implies 2-4z\bar{z} = 0
\implies z\bar{z} = \frac{2}{4} = \frac{1}{2}
\implies |z|^2 = 0.50

